From c9dc1137c93a8d144d7e93b52b7805ec6d15ec03 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ludovic Henry <git@ludovic.dev>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 20:25:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] add the vendored symmetrica library's licence text

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [licence text for a dependency fetched at build time, not part of the upstream sdist]

The wheel's CIBW_BEFORE_ALL_LINUX step builds symmetrica from the pinned
sagemath/sage-package release tarball
(symmetrica-3.1.0.tar.xz, sha256 2efc4b1d047c6fe036453882a20e906ca2bedecae888356c7626447db2b10fd3,
matching build/pkgs/symmetrica/checksums.ini) and links it straight into
sage/libs/symmetrica's compiled extension, but that source tree is
fetched at build time and never lands in the sdist, so nothing carries
its licence notice. build/pkgs/symmetrica/SPKG.rst states the library is
Public Domain; the tarball itself ships no LICENSE/COPYING file to copy
verbatim, so this reproduces that notice instead. Dropping it at the
package root as LICENSE.symmetrica lands it in dist-info/licenses/ via
the same PEP 639 default glob as the package's own LICENSE (gotcha 53).

Signed-off-by: Ludovic Henry <git@ludovic.dev>
---
 pkgs/sagemath-combinat/LICENSE.symmetrica | 16 ++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 16 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 pkgs/sagemath-combinat/LICENSE.symmetrica

diff --git a/pkgs/sagemath-combinat/LICENSE.symmetrica b/pkgs/sagemath-combinat/LICENSE.symmetrica
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..3dc495b
--- /dev/null
+++ b/pkgs/sagemath-combinat/LICENSE.symmetrica
@@ -0,0 +1,16 @@
+Symmetrica is Public Domain.
+
+As stated by its authors (Lehrstuhl Mathematik II, University of
+Bayreuth) at http://www.algorithm.uni-bayreuth.de/en/research/SYMMETRICA
+and reproduced in Sage's own build/pkgs/symmetrica/SPKG.rst:
+
+    License
+    -------
+
+    Public Domain (see the above web site)
+
+No separate LICENSE/COPYING file accompanies the symmetrica-3.1.0.tar.xz
+release tarball (https://github.com/sagemath/sage-package/releases/download/tars/symmetrica-VERSION.tar.xz)
+that this package's CIBW_BEFORE_ALL_LINUX builds from source and links
+into sage/libs/symmetrica's compiled extension, so this notice is
+reproduced here instead.
